WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.485
Not all telemetry is equally useful.

2
00:00:02.485 --> 00:00:11.784
Effective programs evaluate completeness, accuracy, timeliness, consistency, retention, normalization, enrichment, and coverage.

3
00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:18.898
A source can be connected and still fail to provide the fields or history analysts need for a meaningful security question.

4
00:00:18.898 --> 00:00:23.348
Completeness asks whether expected systems and event types are represented.

5
00:00:23.348 --> 00:00:29.455
Accuracy considers whether fields, timestamps, identities, and asset references are trustworthy.

6
00:00:29.455 --> 00:00:38.055
Timeliness measures whether events arrive quickly enough for detection and response, while retention determines how far back an investigation can look.

7
00:00:38.055 --> 00:00:43.214
Normalization helps teams compare different sources through consistent fields and concepts.

8
00:00:43.214 --> 00:00:49.879
Enrichment adds business, asset, identity, vulnerability, threat, or geographic context.

9
00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:56.863
Both can improve analysis, but teams should preserve enough original data to understand how a normalized event was produced.

10
00:00:56.863 --> 00:01:02.072
Coverage analysis connects collection to threats, use cases, and critical services.

11
00:01:02.072 --> 00:01:09.425
Teams document blind spots, monitor source health, test expected events, and review changes in architecture.

12
00:01:09.425 --> 00:01:14.933
Quality is an ongoing operational responsibility rather than a one-time onboarding task.

13
00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:17.228
Source-health measures make quality visible.

14
00:01:17.228 --> 00:01:30.548
Useful measures include expected-versus-reporting assets, event arrival delay, parsing failures, missing fields, sudden volume changes, retention status, and the age of unresolved collection issues.

15
00:01:30.548 --> 00:01:38.790
Owners can use thresholds and review routines to detect degradation before an analyst discovers it during a high-pressure investigation.
